{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790265202,"nonce":"CE3xMgof90N9Ux3xjU8b2sPMgPI=","title":"Python: per-signature instances of closed items","message":"A closed function called from sites passing different argument types gets the join of them, so its body runs on the dynamic path everywhere: pyflate's move_to_front(l, c) is called with a List(Int) once and a List(Str) in its hot loop and joins to Object; scimark LU, deltablue, go, raytrace and richards pass Object-joined parameters to small methods. The item dunders (__getitem__, __setitem__, __contains__, __call__, comparisons) were never closed, and closed operator methods took their parameter types from typed sites although the library's hooks reach them with boxes.\n\nDesign: an instance of a closed item per argument signature seen at a typed call site (key: argument types widened to what a parameter is typed as; a fixed parameter, i.e. the receiver or an annotated one, and a type the item's own parameter already holds, i.e. Object or a subclass of a Class parameter, keyed as the item's), at most four per item, lowered as a separate function and picked by the lowering at the call site. The item's own function stays the join and is what every dynamic entry (hooks, adapters, py$call$m$n, stubs) reaches; the operator, comparison and item dunders and __call__ are closed but keep Object parameters in their own function, so only their instances carry typed keys. A boxed value reaching a Tuple(k) parameter is checked by tag and length and raises as the unpack it stands for. isinstance(x, C) folds to False only when the classes are disjoint both ways, in inference (dead branches), call-site recording and lowering alike.","files":null}]}